# Paths excluded from Semgrep analysis for this repository.
#
# NOTE: committing this file REPLACES Semgrep's built-in default ignore list, so
# every path that must stay unscanned has to be listed explicitly here. That is
# deliberate: it makes the excluded set reviewable in the pull request instead of
# depending on a tool default that can change between releases.
#
# `tests/`, `scripts/` and `tools/` are deliberately NOT listed. They are analysed
# as well, but their findings are reported instead of blocking. The reasoning is
# in docs/security/php-sast.md.
.git/
vendor/
build/
dist/
node_modules/
.phpunit.cache/
.php-cs-fixer.cache/
